=begin
      author: Fizzleworth, Ashraam
        name: fizzsac
        game: gemstone
        tags: sorcerer, sacrifice, shadow essence, combat
    requires: Lich > 5.14.2
     version: 0.7
        note: Written with assistance from Claude (Anthropic).

  This script was designed to help detect whether a target is ready for Sorcerer Sacrifice.

	If you have less than maximum shadow essence, the script will check the target for eligibility.
	If you have maximum shadow essence, it will cast the spell you set as your script variable.
	Mana upkeep via "sacrifice mana" is handled separately by the companion background
	script sac4mana.lic -- run that alongside this one during a hunt.

	Can be run two ways:
	  - From Bigshot, passing an explicit target and spell: ;fizzsac <#targetid> 719
	  - Manually during a hunt, passing just the spell id: ;fizzsac 719
	    Target resolution order: an explicit #id you passed, then your formal
	    /target lock (GameObj.target) if you have one, then the first living
	    NPC in the room. If none of those find anything, the room is
	    considered empty and the script does nothing. Your own minor demon
	    (matched via IGNORE_NPCS = /verlok|animated/i) is never picked as a
	    fallback target, and an explicit #id that resolves to one is refused
	    -- update that regex if you resummon a different demon type.

	Set DEBUG = true/false at the top of the script to toggle the extra
	status messages (room-empty, appraisal) it prints along the way.

	incant() casts via Spell#force_incant instead of raw "release"/"incant"
	fput commands. Lich's Spell#cast internally queues through a shared
	lock (@@cast_lock) so only one script releases/prepares/casts a spell
	at a time across the whole session -- the same mechanism Bigshot's own
	spell commands (e.g. tether) use. Sending raw release/incant fput
	directly bypasses that queue entirely and can cancel whatever Bigshot
	is mid-cast on, which is what was causing Bigshot to keep recasting
	Tenebrous Tether (706) over and over during a hunt.

	A single invocation loops the appraise -> Pain/sacrifice cycle on its own
	(up to MAX_ATTEMPTS times) until the target is dead/gone, the essence is
	harvested, or there's no mana left to weaken it further.

	Sacrifice needs the creature's health down ~2/3+ AND incapacitated
	(gswiki). In practice only the "enticingly frail" appraisal is actually
	sacrificeable -- "susceptible to manipulation" LOOKS ready but the
	sacrifice bounces ("you are thrown back in a small blast"). So:
		- 5 shadow essence already          -> incant <spell_id> at the target
		- target "enticingly frail"          -> Tenebrous Tether (706, for the
		                                        incap + bonus) then sacrifice
		- anything healthier                 -> Pain (711) to weaken it
		- out of mana + not frail            -> one bare sacrifice attempt
		                                        (in case the hunt gutted it),
		                                        then give up -- don't spam
		                                        "not enough mana"

	IMPORTANT: when Fizzleworth is already out of mana (which is exactly when
	sac4mana calls this), fizzsac usually can't Pain a fresh creature down
	far enough on its own -- it depends on the hunt's attack script having
	already beaten the target to ~1/3 health. Rebuilding a depleted essence
	pool needs a dedicated run somewhere you have mana to spare.
=end

DEBUG = true

IGNORE_NPCS = /verlok|animated/i   # your own minor demon / Animate Dead buddy -- never a valid target

def debug(msg)
	echo "[DBG] #{msg}" if DEBUG
end

args = script.vars[1..-1].to_a.compact.map(&:to_s).reject(&:empty?)

explicit_target = args.find { |a| a.start_with?("#") }
spell_id = args.find { |a| a =~ /^\d+$/ }

if explicit_target
	# refuse an explicit id that resolves to our own demon / animate buddy
	et_npc = GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n.id.to_s == explicit_target.delete_prefix("#") }
	if et_npc && et_npc.name.to_s =~ IGNORE_NPCS
		echo "[fizzsac] refusing #{explicit_target} -- that's your own #{et_npc.name}."
		exit
	end
	target = explicit_target
elsif GameObj.target and GameObj.target.name !~ IGNORE_NPCS
	target = "##{GameObj.target.id}"
else
	# No formal /target lock -- fall back to the first living NPC in the room,
	# since most hunting doesn't use an explicit lock at all.
	npc = GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n.status !~ /dead|gone/i and n.name !~ IGNORE_NPCS }
	target = npc ? "##{npc.id}" : nil
end

unless spell_id
	echo "Usage: ;fizzsac <spell_id>  (uses your currently selected target)"
	echo "       ;fizzsac <#targetid> <spell_id>  (explicit target, e.g. from Bigshot)"
	exit
end

SAC_OK   = /You violently shatter the bond on the soul|forming shadow essence/i
SAC_FAIL = /impossible to forge a bond|unable to complete the link|thrown back in a small blast/i

# Attempt the essence harvest. Returns :ok / :fail / :unknown. A "fail" means
# the creature isn't weakened enough (gswiki: health must be down ~2/3+ AND it
# must be incapacitated) -- the caller should Pain it more, not just retry.
def sacrifice(target)
	waitrt?
	waitcastrt?
	r = dothistimeout("sacrifice #{target}", 5,
		Regexp.union(SAC_OK, SAC_FAIL, /Roundtime: \d+|\.\.\. \d+ points/i)).to_s
	waitrt?
	return :ok   if r =~ SAC_OK
	return :fail if r =~ SAC_FAIL
	:unknown
end

# Root the target (helps meet the "incapacitated" requirement + a sacrifice
# bonus). Skipped when it can't be afforded.
def tether(target)
	return unless Spell[706].affordable?
	waitrt?
	waitcastrt?
	Spell[706].cast("#{target}")
end

# @return :cast if Pain went out, :oom if there wasn't mana for it.
def pain(target)
	return :oom unless Spell[711].affordable?
	waitrt?
	waitcastrt?
	Spell[711].cast("#{target}")
	:cast
end

def incant(spell_id)
	spell = Spell[spell_id]

	unless spell.affordable?
		debug("Skipping incant #{spell_id} -- not affordable (mana/spirit/stamina).")
		return
	end

	waitrt?
	waitcastrt?
	result = spell.force_incant
	debug("Incant #{spell_id} result: #{result}")
	result
end

# Full-health -> "..stalwart and formidable" / "firmly bound"; mid ->
# "susceptible to manipulation"; only "enticingly frail" (or weaker) is
# actually sacrificeable -- "susceptible" LOOKS ready but the sacrifice fails
# ("thrown back in a small blast"). So only :frail sacrifices; everything
# above it means "keep hitting it".
def readiness(target)
	status = Lich::Util.issue_command("appraise #{target}", /^The .+? is \w+ in size/, include_end: false, quiet: true, silent: true).join(" ")
	debug("Appraise #{target}: #{status}")
	return :frail  if status =~ /enticingly frail|ready to be severed|hovering (?:on|at) the brink|near death/i
	return :mid    if status =~ /susceptible to manipulation/i
	:tough
end

MAX_ATTEMPTS = 10

############################################
# Main
############################################

if target.nil?
	debug("Not doing anything because room is empty")
else
	echo "Finding: #{target}"

	search = target.delete_prefix("#")
	oom_strikes = 0

	MAX_ATTEMPTS.times do |attempt|
		find = GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n.id == search }
		break if find.nil? or find.status =~ /dead|gone/
		id = "##{find.id}"

		if Resources.shadow_essence.to_i >= 5
			incant(spell_id)
			waitrt?; waitcastrt?; sleep 0.5
			next
		end

		state = readiness(id)
		debug("Attempt #{attempt + 1}/#{MAX_ATTEMPTS}: #{id} -> #{state}, essence #{Resources.shadow_essence.to_i}/5")

		tried_sac = false
		if state == :frail
			tether(id)                       # incap + bonus (free-skips if OOM)
			tried_sac = true
			break if sacrifice(id) == :ok    # essence harvested
			# :fail -> not weak enough after all, Pain more below
		end

		# still standing / sacrifice bounced -> weaken it
		if pain(id) == :oom
			oom_strikes += 1
			# no mana to Pain. If we haven't already tried this iteration, one
			# bare sacrifice in case the hunt gutted it -- then give up. Looping
			# just spams "not enough mana" and eats 3s RT on failed bonds.
			break if !tried_sac && sacrifice(id) == :ok
			if oom_strikes >= 2
				echo "[fizzsac] out of mana and #{id} isn't weak enough to sacrifice -- nothing to do."
				break
			end
		else
			oom_strikes = 0
		end

		waitrt?
		waitcastrt?
		sleep 0.5
	end
end
